  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: MIM curation (#342)
    notes: 'mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch
      -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning*
      than CHEBI:29377 (''sodium carbonate'') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies:
      it files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 ''hydrate'', never under the anhydrous compound,
      which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance
      containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims
      similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record''s own identifier
      are unchanged.'
  - evidence_type: MANUAL_CURATION
    source: MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)
    notes: 'OriginalCultureBotHT S4132/CAS5968-11-6/mass124, primaryNCIT:C80911andPubChem2735133agree
      on sodiumcarbonate monohydrate. No stereochemicalorform ambiguity remains. Noothercurrentowner
      claimsC80911. See the complete identity, mapping, chemistry and synonym assessment
      in reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/authors/science-c/assessments-v2.json;
      owner selector data/ingredients/mapped/Sodium_Carbonate_Monohydrate.yaml. Primary
      source references: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/29377/;
      https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/search?q=sodium%20carbonate%20monohydrate&ontology=chebi,ncit&rows=100;
      https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/5968-11-6/JSON; https://api-evsrest.nci.nih.gov/api/v1/concept/ncit/C80911?include=full;
      https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/US/en/product/sigald/230952; https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureBotHT.
      Captures, exact input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json.
      This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed
      owner bytes withdraw inherited support.'
